Scripts to model the many HVB trips in the summer 2026 run

hists: directory linked to the latest data_monitoring version directory of rootfiles containing CDC_Efficiency and CDC_expert_2

getpedestals.py loops through the run period's collection of root files
               fits the pedestal for each straw and adds it to an array
	       finally draws graphs of pedestal vs run and saves them in pedestals/<n>.png and text into pedestals/ped_<n>.txt


dump_eff.C dumps the efficiency vs straw data from one run into eff.txt
get_all_eff.py runs dump_eff for all runs in the hists directory and saves files into eff_from_histo
               also combines these for ranges where they dont change but that is no longer needed



straw_eff.sh <n>  writes file of run efficiency data for one straw into straw_eff_per_run/eff_<n> 
                  calls rplot.py and writes graph into straw_eff_per_run/eff_<n>.png
                  calls round_efficiency.py, prints results to stdout


suppress_trips.py writes out efficiency files with tripped hvbs at 0
                  and with inefficient straws as specified
		  prints a list of straws with efficiency less than specified value



rplot.py <n> reads the efficiency data and plots the graph




round_efficiency.py <filename> <scalefactor> reads in straw data from straw_eff_per_run/eff_<n> scales it up by defined scalefactor
		    and prints run ranges for efficiency data that are not 1 but 0.95, 0.9 etc   and 0.


update_wiregains.py reads in one hard-coded wiregains file for the run period, loops through the efficiency files
         	    and writes out wire gain files with straw gain set to 0 if the straw efficiency is 0




Iterative process is to set the print threshold in suppress_trips.py
run it and inspect the list of bad straws
look at the pedestal plot
run straw_eff.sh and copy data into suppress_trips.py

gradually reduce the reporting threshold in suppress_trips.py

when finished with efficiency, run update_wiregains.py